 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** Linear with respect to the number of voxels traversed along the ray. The DDA traversal is efficient for sparse volumes as it skips empty space [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** Proportional to the number of active segments. Each segment is a 128³ R8 texture (2 MB). The directory texture is small [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Measured Performance:** Not given in the sources.
-*   **Strengths:** Efficient for sparse voxel models. Avoids floating-point boundary errors by using analytical ray-box intersection. Works well in VR due to correct depth writing [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Limitations:** Requires precomputed inverse model matrix. Performance depends on the density of the voxel model [S1, unofficial].
-*   **When to Use:** Sparse voxel models with large empty spaces. VR applications requiring correct depth for reprojection [S1, unofficial].
-*   **When Not to Use:** Dense voxel models where ray traversal becomes expensive. Models with frequent dynamic changes requiring frequent bound updates [S1, unofficial].
